==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|biðja|lang=non}} (whence also the Danish {{term|bede|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|bedja|lang=sv}} and Icelandic {{term|biðja|lang=is}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|bidjaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{recons|gʷʰedʰ-|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Frisian [[bidda]], Old Saxon [[biddian]] (Dutch [[bidden]]), Old High German [[bitten]] (German [[bitten]]), Gothic {{term|𐌱𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽|tr=bidjan|lang=got}}.

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|bað|bóðu|biðið}}

# to [[ask]], to [[request]], to [[beg]]
# to [[wish]] (e.g. ''[[góðan dag]]'' - good day)
# to [[pray]] to God (''[[Gud]]'')

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-66|b|i|ð|a|ó}}

