==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|biðja|lang=non}} (whence also the Danish {{term|bede|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|bedja|lang=sv}} and Faroese {{term|biðja|lang=fo}}) from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|bidjaną|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with Old Frisian [[bidda]], Old Saxon [[biddian]] (Dutch [[bidden]]), Old High German [[bitten]] (German [[bitten]]), Gothic {{term|𐌱𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽|tr=bidjan|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpɪðja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪðja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bað|báðu|beðið}}

# {{ambitransitive|governs the accusative|optionally ditransitive with genitive|lang=is}} to [[ask]], [[request]] some action of someone
#: ''Ég '''bað''' þig nú bara um [[greiði|greiða]].''
#:: I just '''asked''' you a [[favour]].
# {{intransitive|lang=is}} to [[pray]]
#: ''Ég '''bið''' til [[Guð]]s.''
#:: I '''pray''' to [[God]].

